<task id="021" project="messaging-communication-app-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Regarding-mode `CommunicationTimeline` PCF variant (mirror R1 Timeline PCF + a regarding-resolution path; bound `anchorField`) + production build + solution pack</title>
    <phase>W2 — Record Threads View (Surface 1)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>10</estimated-hours>
    <deps>020</deps>
    <blocks>022</blocks>
    <tags>pcf, deploy, e2e-test</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Packages the extended shared component as a form-bound PCF (React 16/17 platform libraries per ADR-022) with a NEW regarding-resolution path (resolve the host record's `(entityType, id)`); produces a production build + solution ZIP for form placement — a host-affecting deliverable with prescriptive build/pack steps; touches `.ts` PCF code + manifest + solution. ADR-022 (platform libs), ADR-006 (PCF for form binding), ADR-026 (Path-A exception), ADR-028 (auth at boundary) bind; the bound-`anchorField` rule is a hard MUST (R1 lesson); UI tests gate the render. FULL required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>New/variant PCF folder + its own solution ZIP under `src/client/pcf/` — disjoint from the 023 config and the BFF/schema tracks. Depends only on 020 (the component it wraps). This task builds + packs; it does not concurrently edit shared code.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-04</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Package the regarding-mode `CommunicationTimeline` component (task 020) as a **form-bound PCF variant** that resolves the host record's `(entityType, id)` and renders the record's threads-as-groups view. Mirror the R1 `CommunicationTimeline` PCF (`src/client/pcf/CommunicationTimeline/`) — its manifest, `index.ts`, auth-init, and solution structure — adding only the **regarding-resolution path**.

    Requirements:
    - **Mirror the R1 Timeline PCF** structure. Either add a regarding-mode variant control or a mode switch on the existing packaging pattern (state which in notes) — reuse the R1 `authInit.ts` / `hostContext.ts` / App/Host wiring; do NOT invent a new PCF pattern (§11).
    - **Regarding-resolution path** — resolve the **host record's `(entityType, id)`** from the PCF page context (`context.mode.contextInfo` / `context.page` entity name + record id) and pass `mode='regarding'` + `entityType` + `id` to the shared component. This is the one net-new bit vs R1's thread-id resolution.
    - **MUST declare a bound `anchorField` property** — a model-driven-app code component only appears in the form component library if it binds a field (or a dataset). R1 learned this the hard way and now binds the primary Name (`sprk_name`) as a form anchor while reading the record from context. Mirror that exactly: bind `anchorField` to the host record's primary Name; the control reads `(entityType, id)` from context, not from the bound value. Cite the R1 lesson (documented in the R1 Timeline PCF `ControlManifest.Input.xml`).
    - **React 16/17 platform libraries** (ADR-022) — declare React/Fluent as platform libraries (mirror R1: `React 16.14.0`, `Fluent 9.46.2`); MUST NOT bundle React 18; the mounted tree must be 16/17-compatible.
    - **`@spaarke/auth` at the PCF boundary only** — build the `authenticatedFetch` from the Spaarke PCF auth pattern (`authInit.ts`) at the boundary; the shared component never imports `@spaarke/auth` (ADR-028).
    - **No client-side ACS SDK** — the produced bundle MUST NOT contain any `@azure/communication-*` dependency (NFR-04).
    - **Build + pack** — `npm run build:prod` (NOT `npm run build` — AP-1 / root §12), then pack the solution ZIP. **`pac import` is DEFERRED to the owner** — this task produces + validates a build + solution ZIP; task 022 does the 11-form placement/import (or the owner runs it). Document the split.
    - **UI tests** — verify the control renders the regarding-mode grouped view on a form without console errors, is dark-mode correct, and reflects the record's threads.

    Do NOT place the control on the 11 forms here (task 022) — this task produces the buildable + packable PCF variant.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke PCF engineer fluent in the virtual/React PCF pattern, ADR-022 platform libraries (React 16/17), the R1 `CommunicationTimeline` PCF packaging (`authInit.ts` boundary, platform-library manifest, solution ZIP), and resolving the host record `(entityType, id)` from PCF page context. Familiar with the bound-`anchorField` form-component-library requirement (R1 lesson).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A regarding-mode `CommunicationTimeline` PCF exists under `src/client/pcf/CommunicationTimeline/`, mounts the shared component in regarding mode, resolves the host record's `(entityType, id)` from PCF context, declares a bound `anchorField` (primary Name) + platform-library React 16/17 (ADR-022), consumes `@spaarke/auth` at the boundary only (ADR-028), builds clean via `npm run build:prod`, and is packed into a solution ZIP. The bundle contains no ACS SDK (NFR-04). UI tests confirm it renders the grouped regarding view without console errors and is dark-mode correct. `pac import` + 11-form placement is deferred to task 022 / the owner.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      ADR-026 Path-A exception (R1 precedent, carried into R2): R2's message surface is the OOB main form + PCFs — NOT a Code Page. A form-bound PCF is within ADR-006 (PCF for form binding). This task realizes the regarding-mode viewer as a form-bound PCF; cite the Path-A exception in the PR.

      §11 Component Justification — this is a PCF **variant of** the R1 Timeline PCF, not a new pattern. Existing: the R1 `CommunicationTimeline` PCF binds a single thread. Extension: the same packaging + auth boundary + platform libs, with a regarding-resolution path resolving `(entityType, id)` from context and mounting the shared component in regarding mode. Cost-of-doing-nothing: without a form host, FR-04's "regarding-mode Timeline on the record form" has no delivery vehicle. Reuse the R1 PCF's `authInit.ts` / `hostContext.ts` / manifest / solution rather than inventing packaging.

      **Bound `anchorField` (MUST — R1 lesson).** The R1 Timeline PCF `ControlManifest.Input.xml` documents it explicitly: a code component only appears in the form component library if it declares a bound field or a dataset. R1 binds the primary `sprk_name` as a form anchor and reads the record from `context`, not from the bound value. R2's regarding-mode variant MUST do the same — bind `anchorField` to the host record's primary Name so the control is placeable on all 11 forms; resolve `(entityType, id)` from context. (spec FR-04 acceptance + CLAUDE.md MUST rule.)

      ADR-022 boundary: the shared component (020) is authored React-18-friendly for the lib, but PCFs run on the platform React (16/17). The variant must declare platform libraries (mirror R1: React 16.14.0, Fluent 9.46.2) and the mounted tree must be 16/17-safe. If a React-18-only API slipped into 020, fix it in the shared lib (coordinate with 020) — do NOT fork the component into the PCF.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CommunicationTimeline/CommunicationTimeline/ControlManifest.Input.xml (READ/MIRROR — R1 manifest: bound `anchorField`, platform libraries, feature-usage)</file>
