  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test>The control renders the regarding-mode grouped view (threads-as-collapsible-groups) with NO console errors (verified via the `ui-test` skill against the built control / harness).</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Dark mode (ADR-021): the grouped view, group headers, and count badges render correctly when the model-driven app is in dark theme (Fluent v9 tokens pass through).</ui-test>
    <ui-test>The control resolves the host record's `(entityType, id)` from context and shows that record's threads-as-groups (not a single-thread view).</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Bound-field placement: the control is selectable in the form component library because it declares a bound `anchorField` (a control with no bound field/dataset would be hidden).</ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A regarding-mode `CommunicationTimeline` PCF exists under `src/client/pcf/CommunicationTimeline/`, mounts the shared component in regarding mode, and resolves the host record's `(entityType, id)` from PCF context.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The manifest declares a bound `anchorField` property (primary Name) so the control appears in the form component library (R1 lesson cited).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The manifest declares React 16/17 platform libraries (mirror R1); React 18 is NOT bundled (ADR-022).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The produced bundle contains NO `@azure/communication-*` dependency (NFR-04, grep/inspect-verified); `@spaarke/auth` appears only at the PCF boundary, not inside the shared-component chunk (ADR-028).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build:prod` builds clean; a solution ZIP is packed; `pac import` / 11-form placement is explicitly deferred to task 022 / the owner (documented, NOT run here).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">UI tests pass: renders the grouped regarding view without console errors, dark-mode correct, resolves the host record.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on task 020 (the regarding-mode component). Blocks task 022 (11-form placement). This task deliberately stops at build + pack; the `pac import` + placement on all 11 forms is task 022 (or owner-run) — mirror how email-r4/R1 split packaging from owner-run import when the environment auth/import cannot complete in-session. The build + bound-`anchorField` + platform-libs + no-ACS-SDK checks MUST all pass here regardless of the import split.

    If a React-18-only API from task 020 breaks under platform React 16/17, fix it in the shared lib (coordinate with 020) — do NOT fork the component into the PCF (ADR-012 / §11).
  </notes>

